      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix missing in-flight request tracking for `PowerOfTwoPolicy` in regular HTTP routing.\n\nThe regular HTTP router currently creates a `WorkerLoadGuard` only for `cache_aware` and `manual`. However, P2C also relies on `worker.load()` when comparing request loads.\n\nThis change adds `power_of_two` to the existing guard condition, reusing the established request lifecycle management.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Enable `WorkerLoadGuard` for `power_of_two`.\n- Keep the fix minimal without changing other routing policies.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe original issue was reproduced using three local mock workers, with `cache_aware` as a positive control.\n\nThe fix reuses the existing `WorkerLoadGuard` mechanism.\n\nPost-fix validation and automated regression testing have not yet been documented.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nFixes #47868\n\nThis is a narrowly scoped alternative to the broader approach proposed in #47871.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41409152226](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41409152226)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41409152272](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41409152272)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
